  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Partnership**: The player with the **Joker** and the player with the **Ace of Trumps** form the 'Kankei' team. The other three players are the 'Mukankei' team. 2. **The Joker**: The Joker is the strongest card but cannot be played to the first or last trick of a round. 3. **Play**: Counter-clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.",
    Player: "1. **Partnership**: The player with the **Joker** and the player with the **Ace of Trumps** form the 'Kankei' team. The other three players are the 'Mukankei' team. 2. **The Joker**: The Joker is the strongest card but cannot be played to the first or last trick of a round. 3. **Play**: Counter-clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.",
    objective: "Capture 'Point Cards' (A, K, Q, J of each suit). There are 16 points total in the deck.",
    gameplay: "1. **Partnership**: The player with the **Joker** and the player with the **Ace of Trumps** form the 'Kankei' team. The other three players are the 'Mukankei' team. 2. **The Joker**: The Joker is the strongest card but cannot be played to the first or last trick of a round. 3. **Play**: Counter-clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Secret partnership: Joker holder + Ace of trumps = Kankei team',
      'Rotating trumps: â™£â†’â™¦â†’â™¥â†’â™  (repeating)',
      'Joker restrictions: Cannot be played in first or last trick',
      'Joker strength: Beats all cards including trumps when played',
      'Card values: A-K-Q-J = 1 point each (16 total points in deck)',
      'Follow suit: Must follow led suit if possible; can play any card if void',
      'Exchange: The Joker/Ace pair can trade one card to optimize their hands before play begins',
      "Kankei wins with 9+ points; capturing all 16 is 'Gyaku Juuroku' (Reverse 16) worth triple",
    ],
